From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:30:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 107/107] net: wireless: scsc: advertise
 NL80211_FEATURE_MAC_ON_CREATE

cfg80211 passes the NL80211_ATTR_MAC of NL80211_CMD_NEW_INTERFACE on to
add_virtual_intf only when the wiphy sets NL80211_FEATURE_MAC_ON_CREATE,
so the params->macaddr handling added with the wiphy address never got an
address: OpenWrt's station (asked for 0e:..) came up with the hardware
address, the same as the AP's BSSID (0c:..). With the J4 as a repeater
the firmware then gave the AP's clients' authentication frames to the
station vif, hostapd never saw them and every client failed to connect
while the station was up.

Verified on the J4: phy0-sta0 0e:a8:a7:4e:20:76 connected upstream,
phy0-ap0 0c:a8:a7:4e:20:76 with four phones associated and authorized.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c b/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c
index ca1bb1664..a9ff995c6 100755
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/scsc/cfg80211_ops.c
@@ -3596,6 +3596,12 @@ struct slsi_dev                           *slsi_cfg80211_new(struct device *dev)
 	wiphy->features |= NL80211_FEATURE_SCHED_SCAN_RANDOM_MAC_ADDR;
 #endif
 #endif
+	/* cfg80211 hands add_virtual_intf the address user space asks for
+	 * only with this; without it an added station got the hardware
+	 * address, the same as an AP's BSSID, and the firmware then gave
+	 * the AP's clients' frames to the station.
+	 */
+	wiphy->features |= NL80211_FEATURE_MAC_ON_CREATE;
 	return sdev;
 }
 
